  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by the BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude). PDAA is a client engagement (Insilica LLC + EMBSI/ExxonMobil) whose pipeline consumes proprietary EMBSI-provided Excel deliverables (resources/embsi/*.xlsx) with NO public license, and further combines ZINC-derived phthalate compounds (ZINC redistribution requires written permission from its authors) plus ChemHarmony, PubTator and AOP-Wiki. The most-restrictive component governs: the confidential client data alone makes this non-redistributable, so licenseClass=restricted and merckCommercialUse=prohibited. HUMAN REVIEW REQUIRED: this brick contains client-confidential EMBSI data and should NOT be redistributed to any third party (including Merck) absent explicit contractual permission; also confirm the ZINC and ChemHarmony source-license terms.",
